 "status": "COMPOSITION LAW, MEASURED ON THE OPEN CLOCK (zero free parameters, 205 s). At g = 1/5 the traced-loop Cartan ladder is precision-stable end to end: 30- and 50-digit evaluations of F_n agree to 0e+00 for every n <= 172. The one-line chain of 170 hops gives F_170 = 1.3089e-21; the 17 separate insertions multiply to (F_10)^17 = 6.4697e-30; a chain therefore suppresses 2.02e+08 times less than the product of its pieces, which is why the ladder's 17 factors must be insertions on different lines and why a geometric fit of (MG)^170 cannot supply them. The rung-17 suppression carried by the ladder is 6.4697e-30 = 0.5401 x (1/16 pi)^17: the clock deficit 0.964413 raised to the 17th power. The odd-length cancellation used elsewhere is specific to the closure class (odd chains at 1/5: F_3 = 0.2430). VERDICT: the composition law stands on these numbers; the root-clock entries (F_170 = 1.57, (F_10)^17 = 3.9e29, R_17 = 4.0e-30) are floor ratios with no limit at the closure angle (V209).",
